# Who may log in as root over ssh. A public key is not a secret, which is the
# point: with key authentication the image carries nothing an attacker could
# use, whereas a password means the same secret sits in every image ever built.
#
# Mode 0644 is deliberate and sufficient. sshd's StrictModes rejects a file or
# directory that is group- or world-*writable* (it tests mode & 022), not one
# that is readable, and git records only the executable bit — so a 0600 file
# committed here would arrive as 0644 on a fresh clone anyway. Verified on the
# hardware: 0644 here, 0755 on .ssh, 0750 on /root, key login accepted.
ssh-rsa  alekmarinov@gmail.com
